  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "LTD-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-base-change-descent-off-t",
      "title": "Weak unitary descent, Jacquet–Shalika Speh-length collapse, and strong base-change descent off nonsplit sets",
      "statement": "Let E be a CM number field unramified over its maximal totally real subfield at all finite places, let n ≥ 1, and let π be a regular algebraic conjugate self-dual cuspidal automorphic representation of GL_n(𝔸_E) unramified at every nonsplit finite place. (1) Combining the trace-formula dichotomy with partial-norm unitarity and split rigidity rules out nontrivial isobaric partitions, yielding a definite unitary automorphic representation σ of U(n) unramified at all nonsplit places whose local base change matches the Satake multiset of π at all but finitely many split places. (2) For any integer q > 1, d ≥ 1, and z ∈ ℂ, if every shifted parameter satisfies |z q^((d−1)/2 − k)| ∈ (q^(−1/2), q^(1/2)) (0 ≤ k < d), then d = 1; applying this to the Speh base change of σ collapses every Speh length d_i to 1. (3) Split rigidity and cuspidal multiplicity one then force a single cuspidal factor c = 1 with P_0 = π, identifying the split local component of σ with that of π at every split place and matching archimedean infinitesimal characters. (4) For polarized regular algebraic cuspidal representations, this yields strong base-change descent off every finite nonsplit set T.",
      "hypotheses": "A CM field E unramified over E^+ at all finite places, a regular algebraic polarized (hence conjugate self-dual) cuspidal automorphic representation π of GL_n(𝔸_E) unramified at all nonsplit finite places, Speh base change, split rigidity, Jacquet–Shalika local bounds, cuspidal multiplicity one, and the weight-one geometric realizations of WGR-03.",
      "correspondence": "Split rigidity eliminates multi-factor trace-formula outcomes to give weak unitary descent; the open multiplicative width q of the Jacquet–Shalika strip collapses every Speh segment length to d_i = 1; split rigidity and multiplicity one collapse the factor count to c = 1 with P_0 = π, upgrading weak descent to strong base-change descent off T.",
      "dependencies": [
        "WGR-03"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-ltd-speh-collapse",
        "lifts-ltd-strong-descent-match"
      ],
