    {
      "id": "LTD-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-joint-local-weil-closure",
      "title": "Adic Frobenius sections, Galois-invariant crystalline period matrices, joint local Weil closure, and odd-rank crystalline descent assembly",
      "statement": "Let ℓ be a prime, K a finite extension of ℚ_ℓ with Breuil–Kisin prism datum, and E a CM number field. (1) For any Weil–Deligne representation x and element σ, the nth power sum of the characteristic roots at σ equals the trace at σ^n. (2) In an ℓ-adically complete ring R where ℓ is a nonzerodivisor with endomorphism φ fixing ℓ and φ(u) = u^q (q > 0), any pair of matrices α, β with scaled inverses α α' = β β' = ℓ^(2N) I_d and ℓ(α − β) = u^q Γ satisfying ℓ^((2N+1)(n+1)+1) | u^(q^(n+1) − 1) for all n ≥ n_0 admits iterative products P_(n+1) = α φ(P_n) β' converging after rescaling to matrices Q, Q' with Q Q' = ℓ^(2k) I_d, Q ≡ Q' ≡ ℓ^k I_d (mod u), and Q β = α φ(Q); over A_cris this constructs the Frobenius section of every Breuil–Kisin frame. (3) For every crystalline frame, the Galois defect D = Q' ε' σ(Q) − ℓ^(2k) I_d is u-divisible and satisfies the twisted Frobenius equation, hence vanishes, forcing ε' σ(Q) = Q and yielding an invertible Galois-invariant matrix U = f(τ)^(−N) f(Y) Q ∈ GL_d(B_cris) satisfying ρ(g) σ_B(U) = U. (4) Bounding all Hodge–Tate jumps by a single integer N yields crystalline Breuil–Kisin frames on every approximating layer and on the limit lattice, transporting local finite-extension models inside single-trace closure and establishing joint local Weil moment closure. (5) Specializing the trace limit to odd rank, transferring all four local conditions (unramified, de Rham, crystalline, and Weil–Deligne polynomial) via LTD-01 to GL_m cuspidal forms, and patching across an infinite family of quadratic CM extensions assembles the complete odd-rank Galois attachment.",
      "hypotheses": "A prime ℓ, a CM field E, Breuil–Kisin prism data and bounded-pole period rings at finite extensions K/ℚ_ℓ, strong base-change descent off T from LTD-01, and the four-property odd-rank congruence and trace-limit architecture.",
      "correspondence": "Adic matrix iteration builds Frobenius sections in A_cris, u-divisible defect vanishing forces exact Galois invariance and produces an invertible B_cris period matrix, uniform jump bounds build linked crystalline layer frames for joint Weil moment closure, and quadratic CM patching plus strong base-change descent assemble the global odd-rank companion.",
      "dependencies": [
        "LTD-01"
      ],
